# Printed by the compiled program (`chess test --print`) and read against each test's expectations, which say what each step shows; the hosting is Semantics ch. 9 as ruled, with the host document as `$(Path ==> $Elem c)` (Jimmy, 6 November 2026) and ch. 7 as ruled (round 3 ST, TK). A square sits under six hosts (the window, the layers, the column, the row, the border's frame, the grid), each a tick on the way in and a gathered `for` on the way out, so a press on the board runs 13 ticks to idle, and a new word's extent reaches its label a tick after the word (doubt MT), so a key typed into the dialog moves the scene three times. The board is 8 right and 38 down from the window's corner (the title, the column's spacing and the border).
